U|                         yourself.
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
U|                         No, no. Really, I...
O|
N|               Leopold stiffly holds out his arm. A beat. Carlson, stuck, 
N|               takes it WITH HESITATION and is escorted to the dance floor.
O|
N|               They dance. ALL but Leopold and Carlson gaily sing "TA-RA-RA-
N|               BOOM-DE-AY." Leopold, flushed, looks quite smitten. Carlson, 
N|               shy at first, eventually smiles brightly.
O|
C|                                     LEOPOLD
U|                         I suppose we really ought to sing 
U|                         along.
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
P|                              (embarrassed)
U|                         Oh, golly.
O|
N|               They half sing, half speak the TA-RA-RA-BOOM-DE-AY, their 
N|               emphasis on "BOOM." Laughing giddily, their dancing becomes 
N|               freer, picking up speed. The room SPINS. Finally:
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
P|                              (breathless)
U|                         Thank you for the dance. It was 
U|                         lovely. I hope it wasn't too awful 
U|                         for you.
O|
C|                                     LEOPOLD
U|                         Not at all. It was most enlightening.
O|
N|               There is a slight pause. The Grandfather CLOCK strikes 
N|               midnight.
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
U|                         I really must be going.
O|
C|                                     LEOPOLD
U|                         I won't hear of it.
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
P|                              (moving away from him)
U|                         No, I'm quite late as it is.
O|
C|                                     LEOPOLD
U|                         I shall see you to the door...
O|
C|                                     CARLSON
P|                              (stopping him 
P|                              resolutely)
U|                         You're very sweet. I had a wonderful 
U|                         time.
P|                              (she watches him, 
P|                              memorizing his face. 
P|                              Then firmly)
U|                         Goodbye.
O|
N|               Leopold takes a glass of champagne from a passing waiter. He 
N|               watches Carlson pass through the crowd and out the courtyard 
N|               door. He surveys the room. After a moment he follows her.
